Next, because of the horizontal asymptote at \(y = 0\), the degree of the numerator \(p(x)\) must be less than that of the denominator \(q(x)\). Since \(q(x)\) is quadratic, \(p(x)\) must be linear or of lower degree. Let’s assume \(p(x) = bx + d\).

